DTSTART:20241116T150000Z
DTEND:20241116T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T052443Z
UID:2h9ps9d27mj1149hb64n5n9k1m@google.com
CREATED:20240917T165255Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><span>Come join Ashley Wolff\, beloved children’s book autho
 r / illustrator and local artist for a special story time on Saturday\, Nov
 ember 16th\, at 11 am.</span></p><p><span>This event is hosted by Orwell Fr
 ee Library and Addison County Readers\, the sponsor of Dolly Parton’s Imagi
 nation Library (DPIL). All children who enroll in the DPIL receive a free p
 icture book in the mail each month - from birth to five. </span></p><p><spa
 n>Everyone is welcome!  There will be ample time to meet the author and enj
 oy a special snack.</span></p><p><span>For more information\, contact Kate 
 at </span><a href="mailto:orwellfreelibrary@gamail.com" target="_blank"><sp
 an><u>orwellfreelibrary@gamail.com</u></span></a><span> or </span><a href="
 mailto:marita.schine2013@gmail.com" target="_blank"><span><u>marita.schine2
 013@gmail.com</u></span></a><span> for Addison County Readers </span></p><p
 ><span>More…..</span></p><p><a href="https://ashleywolff.com/" target="_bla
 nk"><span><u>Ashley Wolff</u></span></a><span> grew up in Middlebury and by
  age five had declared herself an artist- a craft she has successfully hone
 d over the years by publishing 60+ picture books as an author/illustrator. 
 Some of the award-winning titles are</span><span><i> Baby Beluga\; Stella a
 nd Roy\; Only the Cat Saw\; Me Baby\, You Baby\; Baby Bear Sees Blue\; Who 
 Took the Cookies from the Cookie Jar?\; When Lucy Goes Out Walking\; Compos
 t Stew </i></span><span>and the beloved </span><span><i>Miss Bindergarten</
 i></span><span> Series. Her newest releases are </span><span><i>Wildfire!</
 i></span><span>\, </span><span><i>How to Help a Pumpkin Grow (2021)\, and M
 y Towering Tree</i></span><span> (2024)</span></p><p><span>Ashley‘s passion
  extends to her support of Addison County Readers(ACR) \, the local fundrai
 sing group for Dolly Parton’s Imagination Library (DPIL). As “ambassador” o
 f ACR\, Ashley has generously given her time at presentations at all of Add
 ison County Libraries and beyond. She engages families and young children w
 ith her colorful drawings and explorations of early literacy skills and is 
 masterful in eliciting ideas from the young audience.</span></p><p><span>As
  Ashley Wolff herself says\, “I am in favor of all books\, reading in all p
 laces\, all the time. Dolly Parton's Imagination Library makes this possibl
 e.”</span></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20241105T151847Z
LOCATION:Orwell Free Library\, 473 Main St\, Orwell\, VT 05760\, USA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Story Time with Ashley Wolff\, local author & illustrator 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
