UID:218mcf5j54oa9elf0hv8hqgtl2@google.com
CREATED:20250822T141925Z
DESCRIPTION:Future Land Use Maps &amp\; Housing Targets. <br><br>A member o
 f the Addison County Regional Planning Commission (ACRPC) will be at the Or
 well Free Library on Friday\, 9/12 from 9am - 11am to share information and
  to discuss the Draft Addison County Future Land Use Map and Housing Target
 s for our county and individual municipalities. <br><b>What is this about?<
 /b>  This Future Land Use Mapping is part of Act 181\, Vermont's new land u
 se law passed by the Legislature in June 2024. Act 181 represents a shift i
 n how Vermont approaches development\, resilience\, and natural resource pr
 otection. Act 47 of 2023 (aka HOME Act) introduced new requirements for reg
 ional and municipal plans\, one being the inclusion of housing targets for 
 2030 and 2050\, to ensure an adequate supply of safe and affordable housing
 . <br><b>Why is this important?</b>  Understanding these changes will help 
 your community proactively plan for growth\, align with state policy\, and 
 position itself for future funding and support.<br><br><span>All residents 
 of Addison County are invited to view a large-scale draft Future Land Use M
 ap available at ACRPC during normal business hours.  Or\, if you would like
  to meet one-on-one or with a small group of community members\, contact Ka
 tie Raycroft-Meyer (</span><span><u><a href="mailto:kraycroftmeyer@acrpc.or
 g" target="_blank">kraycroftmeyer@acrpc.org</a></u></span><span>)\, Danelle
  Birong (</span><span><u><a href="mailto:dbirong@acrpc.org" target="_blank"
 >dbirong@acrpc.org</a></u></span><span>)\, or call 802-388-3141 to schedule
  time to meet with a member of ACRPC. </span><br><span>For additional infor
 mation\, visit ACRPC’s </span><span><u><a href="https://acrpc.org/regional-
 programs/act-181/" target="_blank">website</a></u></span><span> to view and
 /or comment on the interactive DRAFT Future Land Use Map\, review Housing T
 argets\, and more.</span>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250822T141925Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY: Regional Planning Survey Visit 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
