UID:7as0k24upgtn9sjd8qhgqn8gr8@google.com
CREATED:20251121T182231Z
DESCRIPTION: Rescheduled because of snow. Now Thursday! Since the discovery
  of planets outside the Solar System (known as exoplanets) 30 years ago\, a
 stronomers have detected and confirmed more than 6000 exoplanets. In this t
 alk I will give an overview of the field of exoplanet science\, including a
  brief discussion of studies that have increased our understanding of exopl
 anets\, recent results from the James Webb Space Telescope\, and future pro
 spects for exciting discoveries\, including the potential detection of life
  on other worlds. <br><span><span>Presenter Kendall</span></span> Sullivan 
 is a postdoctoral researcher in the Department of Astronomy and Astrophysic
 s at the University of California Santa Cruz. They double-majored in Physic
 s and Astronomy at UMass Amherst\, then received their PhD in Astronomy fro
 m the University of Texas at Austin. They study planet formation and evolut
 ion. Outside of work they like to hike\, read\, and cuddle their two cats.
LAST-MODIFIED:20251202T165452Z
LOCATION:Orwell Free Library\, 473 Main St\, Orwell\, VT 05760\, USA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:New Discoveries About Planets Outside of Our Solar System
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
