BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20250116T000000Z
DTEND:20250116T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T052443Z
UID:339vbbfibqlp8n5ubic8aundpm@google.com
CREATED:20250115T171710Z
DESCRIPTION:Virtual presentation - <br>Focusing on the 2024 election\, Poli
 tical Science professor Dr. Shannon McQueen describes “gender frames\,” the
  state of women in politics\, and the partisan gender gap. McQueen combines
  original research with existing studies to explore the impact of gender on
  electoral outcomes.<br><br>Register for the event here:<a href="https://ww
 w.vermonthumanities.org/event/how-can-gender-help-us-understand-elections/"
 >https://www.vermonthumanities.org/event/how-can-gender-help-us-understand-
 elections/</a><br><h4>About the Presenter</h4><p>Dr. Shannon McQueen is an 
 Assistant Professor in the Political Science Department at West Chester Uni
 versity\, specializing in identity politics\, women in politics\, and publi
 c opinion. Her research focuses on gender dynamics\, state politics\, and i
 dentity politics\, with particular emphasis on the role and impact of women
  in the political sphere. Dr. McQueen investigates how women’s involvement 
 and the mobilization of women’s groups shape political landscapes\, as well
  as the institutional\, cultural\, and policy barriers women encounter in t
 heir pursuit of political office.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250115T171710Z
LOCATION:Virtual
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:How Can Gender Help Us Understand Elections?
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
