UID:1vto79oitrvtj09b8tgn0tqeas@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20241005T100000
CREATED:20240528T170949Z
DESCRIPTION:Please joins us on October 5th\, 10am for a musical journey to 
 the land of Queens and Kings as we will meet King Bidgoods and many other m
 embers of the court using a children's picture book by Audrey and Don Wood.
  King Bidgood's refuses to leave his cherished bath tub\, stays there all d
 ay dancing\, singing\, fishing\, playing and eating!  \n\nThe story will be
  read by Kate Hunter\, accompanied  by the trio Umoya: Kaleem Ahmid - Chant
 al Holy - Anna Laufenberg.The group will perform a variety of music on diff
 erent sizes of recorders from the Soprano all the way to the Contra Bass Re
 corder\, about 8ft tall.' \n \nThis program is for all who are interested. 
 Anna Laufenberg is an early music educator and host of our monthly Music wi
 th Anna program
LAST-MODIFIED:20241220T183851Z
LOCATION:Orwell Free Library
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Recorder concert & Music with Anna
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
