DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260225T190000
DTSTAMP:20261031T052443Z
UID:6cl469njv12cea1n60hut608s8@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260225T180000
CREATED:20251229T153237Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Presented by Wolfgang Ziegler </p><p><u>Introduction and dem
 onstration of audio technology developed        during the past 150 years.<
 /u></p>    <p>A set of two presentations follows the path from Edison's    
     purely mechanical audio recording and playback (1877) to        electro
 -mechanical (1920s)\, magnetic (1940s) and digital storage      today (1970
 s). Several groundbreaking inventions        (vacuum tube\, transistor\, co
 mputer... ) along the way made it        possible to reproduce sound with h
 igh fidelity\, longer time        periods and reduced cost - making this fo
 rm of entertainment        available to a wider audience. The introduction 
 includes basic        physics principles governing the production and trans
 mission of        sound. Each era of recording technology will        be br
 ought to life through demonstrations with equipment of        historic impo
 rtance.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260205T214416Z
LOCATION:Orwell Free Library\, 473 Main St\, Orwell\, VT 05760\, USA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Listen. From Edison to MP3
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
