UID:58oel2p837m0jo49k63v0eufs5@google.com
CREATED:20240821T141353Z
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\nLearn about military routes built during the Revolutionar
 y War by touring Orwell's historic road markers. Among the roads discussed 
 will be the Ticonderoga Branch of the Crown Point Road and the Mount Indepe
 ndence-Hubbardton Road. Discover how these roads reveal military action and
  impacted Orwell's road system to date. Our guides will be Jim Rowe\, forme
 r Orwell resident\, founder/owner of Mountainside Maple in Huntington\, VT\
 , and member of the Board of Directors of the Orwell Historical Society\, a
 nd  Orwell resident Walter Phelps. This free event is sponsored by the Orwe
 ll Historical Society\, and all are welcome.
LAST-MODIFIED:20240821T141353Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Historic Military and Town Roads through Orwell\, Vermont
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
