UID:78kpoaljhhjkkbfkliio412ea0@google.com
CREATED:20190727T140201Z
DESCRIPTION:Emma Hart Willard wrote\, "Genuine learning has ever been said 
 to give polish to man\; why then should it not bestow added charm on women?
 "  Willard was an American women's rights activist who dedicated her life t
 o female education in a time when women were not often accepted as thinkers
 .  Dr. Susan Ouellette will discuss this accomplished figure who founded th
 e first school for women's higher education that helped shape the mind of t
 he first suffragette\, Elizabeth Cady Stanton.  Almost two centuries after 
 her first school opened and a century since women's suffrage finally passed
 \, her legacy is ever present.
LAST-MODIFIED:20190727T140202Z
LOCATION:Platt Memorial Library\, 279 Main St\, Shoreham\, VT 05770\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Emma Hart Willard: Pioneer in Women's Higher Ed.
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
