CREATED:20190214T211111Z
DESCRIPTION:Historian Donald Wickman returns to Orwell to discuss a hidden 
 gem in Vermont's history\; the photographic work of Civil War-era Brattlebo
 ro photographer George Houghton.  He captured poignant images of Vermont so
 ldiers in the field\, camp and at home.  This talk explores Houghton's life
  and work and examines some of the images that brought the Civil War back t
 o Vermont via photography.
LAST-MODIFIED:20190214T211111Z
LOCATION:Orwell Free Library\, 473 Main St\, Orwell\, VT 05760\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:George Houghton: Vermont's Civil War Photographer
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
