CREATED:20260312T121947Z
DESCRIPTION:In the years running up to the current 250<sup>th</sup> commemo
 rations of 1776\, the Lake Champlain Maritime Museum has focused its resear
 ch activities on the American Revolution. This presentation will share info
 rmation on a number of previous\, recent\, and current research efforts foc
 used on the Revolutionary War in general\, and the Battle of Valcour Bay (O
 ctober 1776) and its aftermath in particular. Archaeological excavations at
  Valcour Bay\, Arnold’s Bay\, and recent documentation and research efforts
  on the gunboat <em>Spitfire</em> will be discussed. Presented by Chris Sab
 ick\, Lake Champlain Maritime Museum Executive Director. A Vermont Humaniti
 es event hosted by Orwell Free Library.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260312T123910Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Underwater Archaeology of Lake Champlain
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
