 comes Using Alternative Data Collection Methods\n\nDate and Time:\nWednesda
 y\, July 18\, 2018 1:00 pm\, Central Daylight Time (Chicago\, GMT-05:00)\nW
 ednesday\, July 18\, 2018 2:00 pm\, Eastern Daylight Time (New York\, GMT-0
 4:00)\nWednesday\, July 18\, 2018 12:00 pm\, Mountain Daylight Time (Denver
 \, GMT-06:00)\nWednesday\, July 18\, 2018 11:00 am\, Pacific Daylight Time 
 (San Francisco\, GMT-07:00)\n\nEvent number: 666 878 025\nRegistration ID: 
 This event does not require a registration ID\nEvent password: This event d
 oes not require a password.\n\nPlease retain this e-mail. Information about
  preparing for the webinar\, technical requirements and support\, and a per
 sonal "join" link for the webinar are included below.\n\n------------------
 -------------------------------------\nTo join the webinar\n---------------
 ----------------------------------------\n\nOn the day of the event we reco
 mmend you log in to the webinar at least 15 minutes (and up to 30 minutes) 
 in advance using these instructions:\n\n1. Click here to join the online ev
 ent.\nOr copy and paste the following link to a browser:\nhttps://plawebina
 rs.webex.com/plawebinars/onstage/g.php?MTID=e1b12fa48ade6ebe5ffc36d27bf51be
 db\n2. Click "Join Now".\n\nIf you have trouble joining the webinar in one 
 browser\, then be sure to try it in another browser. For example\, if you'r
 e unable to join the webinar in Firefox\, then try it in Internet Explorer.
  Users of Firefox version 26 (or later) or Chrome version 32 (or later) sho
 uld read "Joining a WebEx Meeting on Chrome and Firefox FAQ" at https://sup
 port.webex.com/webex/meetings/en_US/chrome-firefox-join-faq.htm for steps n
 ecessary to enable the WebEx plug-in and join a WebEx event.\n\nYou will be
  connected to the webinar's audio using your computer's speakers or headset
 .\n\nOr\, you may choose to connect to the webinar's audio using your telep
 hone (or Skype\, by following the process outlined by Skype to place calls 
 to land lines):\n\nCall-in toll number (US/Canada): 1-650-479-3208\nAccess 
 code: 666 878 025\n\n------------------------------------------------------
 -\nTechnical requirements & support\n--------------------------------------
 -----------------\n\nPlease review the detailed technical requirements at h
 ttp://www.ala.org/pla/education/onlinelearning/webinars/webextech. Technica
 l support information for the day of the event can be found at http://www.a
 la.org/pla/education/onlinelearning/webinars/support.\n\nTo join the event 
 more quickly\, you can set up Event Manager before the event starts. Go to:
  https://plawebinars.webex.com/plawebinars/ecsetup.php?frommail=1\n\nThe pl
 ayback of UCF (Universal Communications Format) rich media files requires a
 ppropriate players. To view this type of rich media files in the meeting\, 
 please check whether you have the players installed on your computer by goi
 ng to https://plawebinars.webex.com/plawebinars/onstage/systemdiagnosis.php
 \n\n\n-------------------------------------------------------\nFor assistan
 ce\n-------------------------------------------------------\n\nIf you need 
 assistance you can contact PLA Webinars at:\nplawebinars@ala.org\n\nIMPORTA
 NT NOTICE: This WebEx service includes a feature that allows audio and any 
