CREATED:20230905T133445Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><span>All</span><span> </span><span>Morgan</span><span> </sp
 an><span>horses</span><span> </span><span>today trace their lineage back to
  a single</span><span> </span><span>horse</span><span>: a mystery stallion 
 named Figure\, owned by singing teacher</span><span> </span><span>Justin</s
 pan><span> </span><span>Morgan</span><span> </span><span>in the late 18th c
 entury. But who was Figure\, really? What stories have people told about hi
 m in the two centuries since he lived and worked in Vermont? Amanda Gustin 
 of the Vermont Historical Society explores the story of the first</span><sp
 an> </span><span>Morgan</span><span> </span><span>horse</span><span>--a com
 plicated and fascinating story tied up with the idea of Vermont identity\, 
 the relationship between humans and animals\, the creation of American myth
 \, and much more.  A Vermont Humanities Council event hosted by Orwell Free
  Library. Orwell\, Orwell Free Library\, PO Box 92\, 7:00 pm. Kate Hunter\,
  (802) 948-20</span><span>  Reach out at least a week in advance if you nee
 d a special accommodation.</span><br></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230908T184251Z
LOCATION:Orwell Free Library\, 473 Main St\, Orwell\, VT 05760\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Justin Morgan's Horse: Making an American Myth
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
