CREATED:20241003T201628Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>An 8-week series at the Orwell Free Library for local teen m
 usicians.</p><p>Explore the deep cultural roots of blues and jazz and its p
 lace in African American heritage. It’s the only musical art form that can 
 claim to being born in America.  Participants of all levels will be introdu
 ced to the history of jazz and the art of improvisation through a combinati
 on of reading\, listening and playing so bring your instruments!</p><p>Frid
 ay nights in December and January.</p><p></p><p>Sign up your tween or teen 
 (grades 5-12) <a href="https://forms.gle/nZPYviA767G5gMeE9" target="_blank"
 >here</a>. </p><p>This series is presented by jazz musician\, Bob Scarpulla
 .<br><em>Jazz in the Living Room is sponsored by Vermont Humanities Council
 . </em></p><p> </p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250103T164150Z
LOCATION:Orwell Free Library
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Jazz in the Living Room
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
