CREATED:20231010T210611Z
DESCRIPTION:Rocks near Orwell formed under water off the coastline of an an
 cient continent\,\nlocated near the equator! How do we know this? How did w
 e get here from\nthere? Come to this illustrated talk to learn about the am
 azing geology of\nVermont\, and to ask any questions about the environment 
 around us.\nPresented by Professor Emeritus Ray Coish of Middlebury College
 .
LAST-MODIFIED:20240304T152041Z
LOCATION:Orwell Free Library\, 473 Main St\, Orwell\, VT 05760\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Tales of a Lost Ocean in Vermont
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20191109T150000Z
DTEND:20191109T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T052443Z
UID:57mps0hc6i3hi6abp6653qgqv3@google.com
CREATED:20191025T183338Z
DESCRIPTION:Join author\, editor\, & teacher\, Emily Arnason Casey in a wor
 kshop for writers of all kind. Explore the landscape of memory and the plac
 es we can’t return to. Place occupies the heart of many Vermonters and our 
 rural landscapes speak to us. Using visual and textual prompts\, sounds and
  smells\, we delve into the creation of the places that form the scaffoldin
 g of our lives: our childhood homes and haunts\, a favorite grandmother’s k
 itchen\, the barns and woods of youth\, or the landscape of home as it shif
 ts and unfolds into the story of your life.\nBring your notebook and pen\, 
 a treat to share or apple cider if you feel so moved.
LAST-MODIFIED:20191030T171454Z
LOCATION:Orwell Free Library\, 473 Main St\, Orwell\, VT 05760\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Writing Workshop with Emily Arnason Casey
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20230302T000000Z
DTEND:20230302T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T052443Z
UID:12hvb979kccmb5aksf3379i1u1@google.com
CREATED:20230113T134512Z
DESCRIPTION:New date will be announced soon! <br>Miguel Fernández\, profess
 or of Luso-Hispanic Studies at Middlebury College\, will give a presentatio
 n the steamship <i>Independence</i> that sank off Isla Margarita\, Baja Cal
 ifornia\, in 1853 and lost 140 passengers of the 430 on board. <span>Miguel
  will describe the wreck\, tell stories of survivors that were stranded on 
 the island for three days before whaling ships came to their rescue and too
 k them to San Francisco\, and his work with marine archaeologists to identi
 fy the remains of the wreck.</span>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230222T215552Z
LOCATION:Orwell Free Library
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:New date - Tom Sawyer's Wreck: Stories of the Gold-Rush Era Steamsh
 ip Independence (1853) 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
