UID:4kgan5octohvfsivqos6j7m3v1@google.com
CREATED:20190903T165324Z
DESCRIPTION:One hundred years ago\, a full generation before Rosie the Rive
 ter\, women rolled up their sleeves and entered war industries where they h
 ad never been welcome before. They ran powerful machinery\, learned new ski
 lls\, and faced the sullen hostility of the men in the shops.\n\nIn this il
 lustrated lecture\, historian Carrie Brown reveals their courage and their 
 hard work\, and explores how these women helped shape the work that their m
 ore famous daughters would do in the next World War.
LAST-MODIFIED:20190903T165324Z
LOCATION:Platt Memorial Library\, 279 Main St\, Shoreham\, VT 05770\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Rosie's Mom: Forgotten Women of WWI
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
