UID:23l8nbdklfnjavkg40b2ek41ib@google.com
CREATED:20230112T223308Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><span>Do you own a family collection that includes letters\,
  objects\, scrapbooks\, journals and/or photographs? Or maybe a special int
 erest collection? Are you wondering if you should keep it\, or how to organ
 ize it? Taking an objective look and answering some pertinent questions can
  help you decide on a plan of action. This workshop will introduce what mak
 es collections valuable and provide ideas on how to preserve your own colle
 ction. </span><br></p><p><span>This presentation is by Danielle Rougeau\, l
 ong time Middlebury College archivist.</span></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230203T173303Z
LOCATION:Orwell Free Library
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:To Save or Not to Save: What Do I Do with this Stuff?!
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
