UID:2nje7ocu76f7o9vtnhvg3aeen2@google.com
CREATED:20251212T173619Z
DESCRIPTION:<br><br><br><p><span>“We The People” are invited to this presen
 tation by John Vincent to learn the history of printing The American Revolu
 tion\, and to engage in a conversation around an old printing press\, pull 
 a broadside\, and imagine what The Next Revolution could be. At this presen
 tation you will learn that the mission statement of A Revolutionary Press\,
  inspired by the Declaration of Independence\, directs us in our efforts to
  bring about an entirely distinct Revolution for the present and the future
 \, as we listen to\, and print some of today’s lesser known radical and rev
 olutionary visionaries. Everyone at this event will have the opportunity to
  print one of these pieces to help imagine that next Revolution.</span></p>
 This presentation is part of the Orwell Shoreham Libraries Keynote Speakers
  Series and sponsored by the First National Bank of Orwell.
LAST-MODIFIED:20251212T173642Z
LOCATION:Platt Memorial Library\, 279 Main St\, Shoreham\, VT 05770\, USA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:A Revolution Will Not Be Tweeted
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
