DTEND:20261022T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20261031T052443Z
UID:7jands3q98a3abrosfe2jpd2ni@google.com
CREATED:20260922T133112Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><span>Join freshwater snorkeler Graham Montague as he explor
 es the aquatic world beneath Vermont’s lakes\, ponds\, and streams. Through
  underwater videos\, discover the fish\, plants\, and other aquatic creatur
 es that call Vermont’s waters home\, and gain a new appreciation for the be
 auty that exists just below the water’s surface. Graham will share stories 
 and footage from his adventures snorkeling throughout Vermont and offer a u
 nique perspective on the natural world that is often hidden from view.</spa
 n></p><p><b>Bio:</b> Graham grew up in <span>Ohio\, and earned a B.S. in Bi
 ology from Baldwin Wallace University and an M.S. in Natural Resource Ecolo
 gy and Management\, with a focus on fisheries and aquatic ecology\, from Ok
 lahoma State University. He is currently pursuing a Ph.D. at the University
  of Vermont\, where he studies landlocked Atlantic salmon in Lake Champlain
 . In his free time\, Graham creates nature videos and explores New England’
 s underwater environments through snorkeling.</span></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260925T123038Z
LOCATION:Orwell Free Library\, 473 Main St\, Orwell\, VT 05760\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Snorkeling Vermont with Graham Montague
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
