BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260325T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260325T190000
DTSTAMP:20261031T052443Z
UID:6cl469njv12cea1n60hut608s8@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20260325T180000
CREATED:20251229T153237Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><u>A presentation by Wolfgang Ziegler </u></p><p><u>Introduc
 tion and demonstration of audio technology developed        during the past
  150 years.</u></p>    <p><i>A set of two presentations follows the path fr
 om Edison's        purely mechanical audio recording and playback (1877) to
         electro-mechanical (1920s)\, magnetic (1940s) and digital storage  
     </i><i>today </i><i>(1970s). Several groundbreaking inventions        (
 vacuum tube\, transistor\, computer... ) along the way made it        possi
 ble to reproduce sound with high fidelity\, longer time        periods and 
 reduced cost - making this form of entertainment        available to a wide
 r audience. The introduction includes basic        physics principles gover
 ning the production and transmission of        sound. Each era of recording
  technology will        be brought to life through demonstrations with equi
 pment of        historic importance.</i></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260205T214416Z
LOCATION:Orwell Free Library\, 473 Main St\, Orwell\, VT 05760\, USA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Listen. From Edison to MP3
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
